  "notes": "Frozen full run of study p2_lift_linear_complexity_20261110 (PROTOCOL.md sections 2, 9, 10; FREEZE.sha256). Exact integer computation, no timing is a result. Execution route: local host. The isolab-eks route is unavailable from this session (no aws CLI) and the GitHub route takes only ecbench specs, so this is local evidence; the section 9a confirmatory EKS run is open. The run-full command takes about 3 to 4 hours on the 4-core host and has an 8-hour limit, so it runs detached: run the card, then run wait until the receipt status is no longer detached. The cpu-model step runs lscpu in place of reading /proc/cpuinfo, because the card runner takes no shell pipe. The binary bound in binds is the build already on disk before this card; the binary-sha256 step records the digest of the binary this card builds. Re-run (card -02) after the 2026-11-11 container restart, which lost the detached run-full step of F2-RUN-01 (loss ledger: benchmarks/losses/20261111-card-p2-lift-linear-complexity-20261110-f2-run-01-11-run-full.json). The -02 run-full step writes stdout and stderr to results/run-02.stdout.txt and results/run-02.stderr.txt, not results/run.stdout.txt and results/run.stderr.txt, because the card runner opens those logs for truncating write and the stale -01 files stay in place; results/run.json is the same path as in -01 and does not exist yet. The card pins the commit 9465664dbe6ba5757b9cb011192215a00605e8d8; the binds were recomputed from the files on disk on 2026-11-11 and FREEZE.sha256 is unchanged."
